## Authentication

The client supports static tokens, dynamic token providers, and one-time refresh on `401`.

### Static Token

```rust
let sdk = {{.SDKStructName}}::new(ClientConfig {
    base_url: "https://api.example.com".to_string(),
    timeout_ms: Some(30_000),
    auth_token: Some("jwt-token".to_string()),
    auth_token_provider: None,
    refresh_auth_token: None,
    auth_header: None,
})?;
```

### Dynamic Provider + Refresh Callback

```rust
use std::sync::Arc;

let sdk = {{.SDKStructName}}::new(ClientConfig {
    base_url: "https://api.example.com".to_string(),
    timeout_ms: Some(30_000),
    auth_token: None,
    auth_token_provider: Some(Arc::new(|| {
        Box::pin(async { Ok(Some("jwt-from-provider".to_string())) })
    })),
    refresh_auth_token: Some(Arc::new(|| {
        Box::pin(async { Ok("fresh-jwt-token".to_string()) })
    })),
    auth_header: None,
})?;
```

### Runtime Token Management

```rust
sdk.set_token("updated-jwt-token");
sdk.clear_token();
```
